    "result_text": "Full build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change rejects owner creation with **429** once 100+ owners have already been registered today, following the repo's OfficeFloor function-injection pattern (mirroring the existing `CheckCityCapacity` rule).\n\nNew, small, cohesive units (nothing existing was grown):\n- **`CheckDailyLimit`** \u2014 one-method step: counts owners whose `registrationDate` is today and throws when the count reaches `DAILY_LIMIT` (100).\n- **`DailyOwnerLimitException`** \u2014 checked exception so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n- **`DailyOwnerLimitHandler`** \u2014 escalation handler responding `HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` (429).\n- **`...DailyOwnerLimitException.yml`** \u2014 wires the exception to the handler.\n\nOnly one existing file was edited: `owners.POST.yml` gained a `checkDailyLimit` step inserted after `checkCityCapacity`. New owners already default `registrationDate` to today via `OwnerMapper`, so the count naturally includes each fresh create.\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` and the full suite pass.",
